<title>CHILE: Chilean firm sells small Can-Can gold mine.</title>
<headline>Chilean firm sells small Can-Can gold mine.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean coal firm Compania de Carbones de Chile Cocar SA said it has decided to sell its 60 percent stake in the small Minera Can-Can gold mine.</p>
<p>The company, which is 45-percent owned by industrial group Compania de Petroleos de Chile SA, will also sell its nine percent stake in power company Empresa Electrica Guacolda, said the statement to the Chilean SEC.</p>
<p>The shares in both companies will first be offered to Cocar's shareholders, it said.</p>
<p>Can-Can produced 45,000 ounces of gold last year and 668,000 ounces of silver.</p>
</text>
